      "message": "Ouch. If we are going to allow multiple pending requests for the same type, then I think this code needs to be more explicit about it. This remove exists to enforce the invariants (on older releases, \"one request per type\", in newer releases \"only one fuzzy-matching request at a time\").\n\nSo we should do something like:\n- If the request is for bluetooth, then accept it regardless, and make it clear in other parts of the code that duplicate requests can happen, and support them.\n- If not, remove all other pending requests.\n\nTBH it seems simpler not to attempt this at all, and just say that this class will never allow duplicate requests. For the special case of bluetooth, we could either change the behaviour, or have the caller deal with it.",
